WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.820
Turn your dashboard skills into a paid service.

2
00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:07.460
This is the video for module three of Advanced Excel and Dashboards.

3
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:18.040
Most Excel projects that go wrong do so before a single formula is written. The builder made charts when the owner really wanted to know who owes money.

4
00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:23.150
A one-page specification fixes that, and both sides sign it.

5
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.380
Then you price the whole job, not just the formulas.

6
00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:35.910
And you show proof. Clients rarely ask about your certificate first. They ask: have you done something like this before?

7
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.370
A discovery call usually takes 30 to 60 minutes. Start from the decisions the owner makes each week or month.

8
00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:51.120
Ask how the report is made now and how long it takes. That time saved supports your price.

9
00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:58.320
Ask where the data comes from, and ask to see a sample of it, even ten rows with names removed.

10
00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:02.180
Ask who reads the dashboard and who updates it.

11
00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:19.940
And check the exact version under File, Account. XLOOKUP is not available in Excel 2016 or 2019. Mrs Bello's school laptop runs Excel 2019, so her builder plans INDEX and MATCH instead.

12
00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:33.290
Business data often holds personal data: customers' phone numbers, pupils' records, staff salaries. Nigeria's Data Protection Act 2023 sets rules for this.

13
00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:42.300
At the school, pupil names stay on the school's computer. The builder works on a copy with names replaced by pupil ID numbers.

14
00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:49.140
Agree in writing how files are shared. A business cloud folder, not personal WhatsApp.

15
00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:53.010
And when the project ends, delete your copies.

16
00:01:54.260 --> 00:02:03.480
First, her rate. A target of 400,000 naira a month over about 50 billable hours means at least 8,000 naira per hour.

17
00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:16.970
She estimates each phase: discovery, cleaning data, formulas, layout, testing, and instructions with training. That is 31 hours. A 20 percent contingency brings it to 37.

18
00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:26.800
37 hours at 8,000 is 296,000 naira, so she quotes 300,000 for the fixed project.

19
00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:30.290
Half on signing, half on handover.

20
00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:41.330
She also shows the value. The bursar spends about 6 hours each Friday on reports. The tool should cut that to under 1 hour, about 60 hours saved per term.

21
00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:49.380
Write this split in your proposal. Fixing errors, small adjustments and two rounds of revisions are included.

22
00:02:50.630 --> 00:03:03.750
A new report, a new data source or a redesign is a change request. Do not say yes or no straight away. Send a short note with the extra hours, cost and new date, and let the client decide.

23
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:11.980
Invoice from a business account or a recognised payment platform, and confirm every transfer in your own banking app.

24
00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:23.020
Watch for clients who overpay and ask you to refund the difference. It is a common fraud pattern. Never share your banking login or one-time passwords.

25
00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:31.290
Share screenshots or a PDF for approval, and send the full working file once the final payment is confirmed.

26
00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:37.590
Choose one type of client: pharmacies, schools, distributors or cooperatives.

27
00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:53.710
Build dashboards with realistic sample data, and say clearly it is sample data. Write each as problem, approach and result, in about 150 words. Never publish a client's real figures without written permission.

28
00:03:54.960 --> 00:04:03.820
Contact businesses of that type with personal messages that name one problem you noticed. Start close to home, where trust already exists.

29
00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:15.780
Deliver, collect a testimonial, and ask for referrals. Track it all in your own workbook. If 40 messages lead to 4 calls, you need about 10 messages per call.

30
00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:28.650
Remember. Start from the client's decisions. Check the version. Get the specification signed, then price every phase with a contingency. And let your portfolio do the talking.

31
00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:41.020
Run a practice discovery with a real business and write a one-page specification. Price it and write a one-page proposal. Then send your first outreach message this week.

32
00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:43.520
Now continue with the lessons below.
